From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:50:58 +0000
Subject: PCI: Disable ASPM on ASMedia ASM1061 SATA controllers

Since v6.18 the kernel enables L0s and L1 by default on devicetree
platforms.  On ODROID-HC4 the link to the ASM1061 then dies in L1 while
the disks behind it spin up after s2idle resume - 6 of 21 cycles - and
the controller answers again only after PERST#.  With L1 left off
(pcie_aspm.policy=performance) none of 15 cycles failed.

Disable L0s and L1 on it, as done for the ASMedia ASM1083 bridge.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index 0500d5fd4f11..77d3ab25bbbc 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -2525,6 +2525,8 @@
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_FREESCALE, 0x0451, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_PASEMI, 0xa002, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_HUAWEI, 0x1105, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
+/* ASM1061 loses the link in L1 as the disks behind it spin up after resume */
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ASMEDIA, 0x0611, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
 
 /*
  * Some Pericom PCIe-to-PCI bridges in reverse mode need the PCIe Retrain
